  "verbalization": "Promazine is implicated in the pathogenesis of the common cold through a chain of indications that link it to Atopic Conjunctivitis, which in turn is associated with several drugs, including Chlorcyclizine, Diphenylpyraline, and Pheniramine. These drugs are all indicated for Atopic Conjunctivitis, a condition that is not directly linked to the common cold but may share underlying mechanisms, such as inflammation or allergic responses. The indirect pathway suggests that Promazine may influence the body's inflammatory response, potentially contributing to the development of common cold symptoms. The evidence is supported by the presence of multiple indirect pathways, each linking Promazine to a different drug that is associated with Atopic Conjunctivitis, which in turn is linked to the common cold. The strength of the evidence is reinforced by the consistent presence of Promazine in these indications, though the exact mechanism by which Promazine affects the common cold remains unclear.",
